\DOC SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a goal of the form {t subsumed u} relating two state-change
({MAYCHANGE}-style) relations, closing it outright.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments.
{
   A ?- t subsumed u
   ==================  SUBSUMED_MAYCHANGE_TAC
      (no subgoals)
}
\noindent The assumptions {A} are left untouched and play no role in the
observed traces, which include goals with no assumptions as well as goals
carrying large sets of symbolic-execution assumptions. The two sides may be
built from register, flag, event and memory components combined with {,,} and
nested parenthesised groups, including cases where the right-hand side covers
memory regions or component lists larger than, or differently decomposed from,
the left.

\FAILURE
Fails on subsumption goals whose right-hand side is not of the form the tactic
can match against — for instance when the covering relation is given as an
explicit lambda-abstraction over the two states rather than a {MAYCHANGE}-style
combination, or when the left-hand components are not covered by the right-hand
side. Such failures arise inside the tactic's own matching and rewriting
machinery rather than from any supplied argument, since it takes none.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the only successful outcome is this one: goals of this
subsumption shape being closed.

\ENDDOC
